# Clover ICNSS: IRQ-safe lookup and serialized firmware lifecycle
#
# CE hard IRQs call icnss_get_ce_id(), so backend lookup must never take
# a mutex. Pair acquire/release publication with client/IRQ teardown and
# disable manual sysfs unbind while dependent clients can still call us.
# Serialize client callbacks, firmware work and SSR against unregister.
# Vote power before WLFW initialization, and never drop rails or reclaim
# MSA underneath a probed client. Notify FW_DOWN before modem shutdown.
# Require physical reserved MSA memory: a DMA-IOMMU IOVA is not an SCM PA.
# Do not infer successful ownership transfer from an SCM -EINVAL error.
# Keep the backend and QMI alive until client teardown is complete, and
# avoid sleeping locks in noirq PM callbacks. Restore per-unit factory
# MAC handling instead of embedding one tablet's address in shared DTS.
#
